# ---------------------------------------------------------------- S2.2 frames
S22 = sh(
    "S2.2",
    r"Replacing scalars by arrays and giving every vertex of the network an invertible frame $D_v$, the network implements $D_{\rm out}\,\mathsf S_\Omega\,D_{\rm in}^{-1}$, and a route from input role $w$ to output role $\rho(w)$ applies $\varepsilon_wD_{\mathrm{sink}(\rho(w))}D_{\mathrm{source}(w)}^{-1}$.",
    "Let every gate act pointwise on aligned arrays, store the array of a wire in the frame of its current vertex, and use linearity to move the gate past the common frame, so that each edge only changes frames and the intermediate frames telescope.",
    mot("The scalar network only fixes the signed exchange; a common frame at each gate lets the gate keep acting pointwise while the edges change the representation cheaply.",
        "recoverable"),
    [
        inf("S2.2.1",
            r"Replace each scalar by an array in $R^\Omega$ over a common finite address set $\Omega$ and apply each gate pointwise at every address; call the resulting network $\mathsf S_\Omega$.",
            r"set common to all wires.  Replace each scalar by an array in $R^\Omega$, and"),
        inf("S2.2.2",
            r"At each source, gate and sink $v$ assign an invertible $R$-linear operator $D_v$ (its frame) on $R^\Omega$; all incidences of a gate share one frame, and on an edge from $u$ to $v$ the operator $D_vD_u^{-1}$ changes the stored array from $D_ug$ to $D_vg$.",
            r"assign an invertible $R$-linear operator"),
        inf("S2.2.3",
            r"The supplied input $f$ needs no preprocessing: its logical interpretation is defined to be $g=D_{\rm in}^{-1}f$, with $D_{\rm in}=\bigoplus_wD_{\mathrm{source}(w)}$ and $D_{\rm out}=\bigoplus_wD_{\mathrm{sink}(w)}$.",
            r"For a supplied physical input $f$, define its logical interpretation to be"),
        inf("S2.2.4",
            r"By $R$-linearity $\sum_jc_jD_v\varphi_j=D_v(\sum_jc_j\varphi_j)$, so the common frame commutes with the pointwise gate and the invariant 'stored array $=D_v$ applied to the logical array' continues from sources to sinks.",
            r"Thus the common frame commutes with the pointwise gate, and",
            salient="Because a pointwise linear gate commutes with a frame shared by all its wires, the cost of the whole network is the cost of its edges: every gate costs one scan."),
        inf("S2.2.5",
            r"The implemented operator is $D_{\rm out}\,\mathsf S_\Omega\,D_{\rm in}^{-1}$ (the common-frame identity).",
            r"D_{\rm out}\,\mathsf S_\Omega\,D_{\rm in}^{-1}."),
        inf("S2.2.6",
            r"If the scalar network is a signed role permutation sending input role $w$ to output role $\rho(w)$ with sign $\varepsilon_w$, that route applies $\varepsilon_wD_{\mathrm{sink}(\rho(w))}D_{\mathrm{source}(w)}^{-1}$ to its input array, including the routes of auxiliary roles, so the endpoint frames alone fix the array operator and the intermediate frames can be chosen to make each edge cheap.",
            r"$\varepsilon_w$, that route applies"),
    ],
    page="frames-on-arrays",
    frm=["bank-exchange-network", "matrices-invertibility-and-rank", "permutations-and-bijections"],
)

