    [
        inf("S2.5.2.1",
            r"Choose the factorizations for all matrices of a fixed finite collection once and for all, together with their factors and inverses, and an odd prime $q$ avoiding every denominator and every numerator of a diagonal entry; all identities then specialize to $\mathbb Z/q^b\mathbb Z$ and the triangular factors stay invertible.",
            r"Choose the factorizations of Lemma~\ref{lem:lower-lower} for all matrices"),
        inf("S2.5.2.2",
            r"A lower triangular transformation of $H$ or of $D$ costs $O(V)$: update the coordinates in descending physical order, at coordinate $i$ multiplying by its diagonal unit and adding a fixed combination of earlier coordinates that still have their original values.",
            r"A lower triangular transformation of $H$, or of $D$, costs $O(V)$:"),
        inf("S2.5.2.3",
            r"For $A=E_1\Pi E_2$: transform $D$ by $E_2$ and $H$ by $E_1^{-1}$, add $\Pi D$ to $H$, then transform $H$ by $E_1$ and $D$ by $E_2^{-1}$.",
            r"For $A=E_1\Pi E_2$, first transform $D$ by $E_2$ and $H$ by $E_1^{-1}$,"),
        inf("S2.5.2.4",
            r"Each one at position $(i,j)$ of $\Pi$ calls for $H_i\leftarrow H_i+D_j$, implemented by $D_j\leftarrow D_j+H_i$, then the swap $(H_i,D_j)\leftarrow(D_j,H_i)$, then $D_j\leftarrow H_i-D_j$.",
            r"(H_i,D_j)\leftarrow(D_j,H_i),\qquad"),
        inf("S2.5.2.5",
            r"On an initial pair $(h,d)$ this sequence yields $(h,d+h)$, then $(d+h,h)$, then $(h+d,d)$; the first and last updates target a later field controlled by an earlier one and cost $O(V)$, so each one of $\Pi$ costs exactly one interchange and there are $a$ ones.",
            r"field.  On an initial pair $(h,d)$ this sequence yields $(h+d,d)$."),
    ],
    page="matrix-shear-cost",
    frm=["lower-triangular-factorization", "controlled-shifts", "multitape-streams", "modular-arithmetic-and-congruences", "euclidean-algorithm-and-modular-inverses"],
